(7658918, 1247435, 251422, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by roz:</b></div><hr/><i> its so funny .. and interesting .. that some of the things that i really liked in this photo were not the things other ppl liked .. i particularly loved the spillage .. i could just see myself licking the side of the cup to get the most chocolate .. that could have been the yummiest bit to me ..  dont let anything go to waste i reckon ... and you turned out to be a temptress ... !! </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yes the spillage makes it more realistic and appealing IMHO.  I used to do a lot of food photography and in many instances the messier the more realistic.  Thanks for your comment</td>', 'Originally posted by roz: its so funny .. and interesting .. that some of the things that i really liked in this photo were not the things other ppl liked .. i particularly loved the spillage .. i could just see myself licking the side of the cup to get the most chocolate .. that could have been the yummiest bit to me ..  dont let anything go to waste i reckon ... and you turned out to be a temptress ... !!  Yes the spillage makes it more realistic and appealing IMHO.  I used to do a lot of food photography and in many instances the messier the more realistic.  Thanks for your comment', '2020-04-17 06:57:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658919, 1247435, 251422, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lydia:</b></div><hr/><i> I wish the cocoa weren''t running down the mug.   Seems somehow "dirty" to me.  <br/> <br/>But, golly!  I totally LOVE the rest of it!  Perfectly set up and captured. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>The spliiage was intentional.  In some Types of food photography we try and make it realistic.  In this case I though the spillage added to the photo.  Glad you liked it though.  Thanks!</td>', 'Originally posted by Lydia: I wish the cocoa weren''t running down the mug.   Seems somehow "dirty" to me.   But, golly!  I totally LOVE the rest of it!  Perfectly set up and captured.  The spliiage was intentional.  In some Types of food photography we try and make it realistic.  In this case I though the spillage added to the photo.  Glad you liked it though.  Thanks!', '2020-04-17 06:59:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(7658920, 1247435, 251422, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lydia:</b></div><hr/><i> I wish the cocoa weren''t running down the mug.   Seems somehow "dirty" to me.  <br/> <br/>But, golly!  I totally LOVE the rest of it!  Perfectly set up and captured. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>In certain types of food photography, it is meant to look more realistic.  It was intentional.  Glad you liked the photo minus the spillage!  Thanks appreciate your comments.</td>', 'Originally posted by Lydia: I wish the cocoa weren''t running down the mug.   Seems somehow "dirty" to me.   But, golly!  I totally LOVE the rest of it!  Perfectly set up and captured.  In certain types of food photography, it is meant to look more realistic.  It was intentional.  Glad you liked the photo minus the spillage!  Thanks appreciate your comments.', '2020-04-17 07:00:51.000000', NULL, 0),
